  "decoded_statement": "Let $S_m$ be the symmetric group, let $\\Delta(S_m)$ be the simplex of probability distributions on $S_m$, and let $P_m\\subseteq\\Delta(S_m)$ be the locus hit by product measures. A **pure cycle** is a permutation with exactly one nontrivial cycle and all other points fixed. Write\n\n$$\nC(m)=\\sum_{k=2}^m \\frac{m!}{k\\cdot (m-k)!}\n$$\n\nfor the number of pure cycles in $S_m$.\n\n**Dimension conjecture.** For all $m$, the dimension of $P_m$ is exactly $C(m)$.\n\nThe paper proves the upper bound $\\dim P_m\\leq C(m)$ and verifies equality for $m\\leq 7$, but the equality is conjectural for general $m$.",
